WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.119
Week 11: Food, Markets, and Restaurants. buy food order a meal handle dietary needs and problems

2
00:00:07.119 --> 00:00:29.820
Read for the situation. En el mercado, Sara compara precios y compra verduras frescas. Más tarde pide el menú del día, pregunta por los ingredientes y explica que no puede comer nueces. At the market, Sara compares prices and buys fresh vegetables. Later she orders the daily special, asks about the ingredients, and explains that she cannot eat nuts.

3
00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:38.561
Read again for evidence. Identify who acts, what changes, when it happens, and which words establish the relationship between events.

4
00:00:38.561 --> 00:00:44.549
Reading activities. Reading activity 25; Reading activity 26

5
00:00:44.549 --> 00:00:52.458
Retell. Without looking back, give the main idea, three supporting details, and one reasonable inference in Spanish.

6
00:00:52.458 --> 00:01:19.441
Model language. Quisiera probar el plato del día. — I would like to try the daily special. ¿Cuánto cuesta un kilo de tomates? — How much does a kilogram of tomatoes cost? Para mí, una sopa sin carne. — For me, a soup without meat. El camarero nos trae la cuenta. — The waiter brings us the bill. Disculpe, pedí agua y no refresco. — Excuse me, I ordered water, not soda.

7
00:01:19.441 --> 00:01:29.361
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
